    <h1>Awesome Video</h1><p class="list-description">A curated list of awesome video tools, frameworks, libraries, and learning resources</p><h2>Community &amp; Events</h2><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.tvtechnology.com/features/2025-nab-show-cinecentral-fuses-tools-and-technique" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2025 NAB Show: CineCentral</a></div><div class="resource-description">The 2025 NAB Show&#39;s CineCentral focuses on the interplay between tools and techniques in storytelling across media formats. It offers hands-on education through live demos, expert-led training, and interactive workshops, covering topics like scene blocking, emotional camera work, and technical skills essential for video production.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video production</span><span class="tag">storytelling</span><span class="tag">workshops</span><span class="tag">training</span><span class="tag">media formats</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.mile-high.video/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACM Mile-High Video</a></div><div class="resource-description">ACM Mile-High Video conference in Denver covering video coding and streaming research with peer-reviewed talks and an engineer tutorial track (AV2/VVC/AV1).</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.mile-high.video/technical-program" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACM Mile-High Video 2025</a></div><div class="resource-description">The ACM Mile-High Video 2025 conference features a comprehensive technical program covering topics such as CDN-based video streaming, content-adaptive encoding, video enhancement, AI-generated content, and film grain technology. It includes presentations, panels, and discussions led by industry experts.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">ACM</span><span class="tag">Mile-High Video</span><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">video streaming</span><span class="tag">AI</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://2026.acmmmsys.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACM MMSys 2026</a></div><div class="resource-description">Official site for the 17th ACM Multimedia Systems Conference with co-located NOSSDAV and MMVE workshops on streaming and networked video.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://2026.acmmmsys.org/call-for-papers" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACM MMSys 2026 — Call for Papers</a></div><div class="resource-description">Multimedia Systems Conference CFP detailing research, open dataset, and open-source software tracks — the main academic venue for streaming systems work.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://nossdav.org/2026/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACM NOSSDAV 2026 — Workshop on Network and OS Support for Digital A/V</a></div><div class="resource-description">36th edition of the long-running ACM workshop on network/OS support for digital audio and video: immersive media delivery, ML for streaming, cloud-based coding.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://aospandaaos.github.io/meetup.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AOSP and AAOS Meetup Archive</a></div><div class="resource-description">A comprehensive archive of meetings focused on the Android Open Source Project (AOSP) and Android Automotive OS (AAOS). The archive includes slides and videos from various talks, providing valuable insights into Android development and related technologies.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">AOSP</span><span class="tag">AAOS</span><span class="tag">Android development</span><span class="tag">technical talks</span><span class="tag">developer resources</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://developer.apple.com/forums/topics/media-technologies/streaming" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Developer Forums - Media Technologies</a></div><div class="resource-description">Apple&#39;s Developer Forums offer a dedicated section for Media Technologies, including streaming. Developers can engage in discussions about HTTP Live Streaming (HLS), AVFoundation, and other Apple media technologies, making it a crucial resource for those developing on Apple platforms.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Apple</span><span class="tag">developer forum</span><span class="tag">media technology</span><span class="tag">HLS</span><span class="tag">AVFoundation</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://github.com/citizen00147/atlanta-tech-resources" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Atlanta Tech Resources</a></div><div class="resource-description">A curated collection of groups, events, and opportunities for developers in the Atlanta, GA area. This repository serves as a comprehensive guide to active tech meetups, affordable conventions, and networking opportunities, making it easier for developers to connect and collaborate.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">developer meetups</span><span class="tag">Atlanta</span><span class="tag">tech events</span><span class="tag">networking</span><span class="tag">community resources</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://github.com/MartinRosenberg/Awesome-Tech-Communities" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Awesome Tech Communities</a></div><div class="resource-description">A curated list of tech communities across various regions, including those focused on video technology. This resource helps developers find and connect with local and global tech groups, fostering collaboration and knowledge sharing.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">tech communities</span><span class="tag">developer meetups</span><span class="tag">networking</span><span class="tag">collaboration</span><span class="tag">resources</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://github.com/elizabethsiegle/Bay_Area_tech_meetups" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bay Area Tech Meetups</a></div><div class="resource-description">A comprehensive list of tech meetups in the San Francisco Bay Area, covering topics like mobile development, iOS, AI, and more. It provides details on meetup topics, locations, and schedules, aiding developers in finding relevant community events.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Bay Area</span><span class="tag">tech meetups</span><span class="tag">developer community</span><span class="tag">networking</span><span class="tag">event listings</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://bitmovin.com/blog/video-technology-developers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bitmovin Community Site</a></div><div class="resource-description">Bitmovin&#39;s community site offers a wealth of public projects, open and solved questions, forums, and hundreds of resources for video technology developers. It&#39;s an excellent location to exchange information with peers and share opinions about Bitmovin&#39;s products and video streaming technologies.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">developer community</span><span class="tag">forum</span><span class="tag">resources</span><span class="tag">Bitmovin</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.meetup.com/bos-video-technology/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BOS Video Technology Meetup</a></div><div class="resource-description">The BOS Video Technology meetup in Boston is for individuals interested in the technology behind video playback, storage, and delivery. Topics include HTML5 video, streaming, transcoding, codecs, advertising, open standards, and CDNs. The group focuses on the engineering aspects of video technology.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">streaming</span><span class="tag">transcoding</span><span class="tag">codec</span><span class="tag">engineering</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://webinar.brightcovegallery.com/bcovkorea2023-en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brightcove Global Streaming Technology Summit 2023</a></div><div class="resource-description">The Brightcove Global Streaming Technology Summit 2023, held on December 14, 2023, focused on how media companies in South Korea can expand their global footprint using the latest streaming technologies. The event featured discussions on the global FAST market, choosing the right streaming solutions, and the importance of streaming technology for global success.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">streaming technology</span><span class="tag">global expansion</span><span class="tag">FAST market</span><span class="tag">media companies</span><span class="tag">video streaming</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://community.usa.canon.com/t5/Video/ct-p/videosolutions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Canon Video Forums</a></div><div class="resource-description">The Canon Video Forums provide a platform for discussions related to Canon&#39;s video products, including camcorders, professional video equipment, and video accessories. Users can seek advice, share experiences, and discuss technical aspects, making it a valuable community for developers and professionals working with Canon&#39;s video technology.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">Canon</span><span class="tag">developer forum</span><span class="tag">video equipment</span><span class="tag">video accessories</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://github.com/cncf/communitygroups" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CNCF Community Groups</a></div><div class="resource-description">Managed by the Cloud Native Computing Foundation, this repository organizes community groups (formerly meetups) focused on cloud-native technologies. It offers resources for organizing and participating in community events, including training sessions and support for event management.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">CNCF</span><span class="tag">cloud-native</span><span class="tag">community groups</span><span class="tag">meetups</span><span class="tag">developer resources</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://groups.google.com/a/webmproject.org/g/codec-devel" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Codec Developers - Google Groups</a></div><div class="resource-description">The Codec Developers Google Group is a mailing list for discussions related to codec development, including topics on libvpx and AV1. It&#39;s a platform for developers to share information, ask questions, and collaborate on codec-related projects.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">codec development</span><span class="tag">libvpx</span><span class="tag">AV1</span><span class="tag">developer forum</span><span class="tag">video encoding</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://commcon.xyz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CommCon</a></div><div class="resource-description">Open-source real-time communications community conference covering FreeSWITCH, Asterisk, Janus, Jitsi, Kamailio, and WebRTC stack.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://compress.cafe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">compress.cafe — Encoding Community Resources</a></div><div class="resource-description">Curated index of active video-encoding Discord communities and practitioner guides from the SVT-AV1-PSY / HDR encoding scene.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://github.com/conferencexp/conferencexp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ConferenceXP</a></div><div class="resource-description">ConferenceXP is an open-source video conferencing and collaboration platform developed by Microsoft Research. It supports low-latency, high-fidelity conferencing applications and is optimized for multicast networks, making it suitable for academic, government, and research networks.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video conferencing</span><span class="tag">collaboration</span><span class="tag">open-source</span><span class="tag">Microsoft Research</span><span class="tag">multicast</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://creativecow.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative COW</a></div><div class="resource-description">Creative COW is a website of support communities for digital video, video editing, and media production professionals in broadcasting, motion graphics, visual effects, and film. It provides over 60 online support discussion forums spanning a wide range of professional video tools and software, along with over 1,000 free text and video tutorials, podcasts, and other resources for video professionals.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video editing</span><span class="tag">media production</span><span class="tag">broadcasting</span><span class="tag">motion graphics</span><span class="tag">visual effects</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PSdhW-R9u6s&amp;list=PLkyaYNWEKcOfntbMd6KtHhF7qpL9hj6of" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2017</a></div><div class="resource-description">2017 Demuxed talks &amp; presentations</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">presentations</span><span class="tag">talks</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bfK_f7GBA8s&amp;list=PLkyaYNWEKcOfARqEht42i1P4kBemzEV2V" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2018</a></div><div class="resource-description">2018 Demuxed talks &amp; presentations</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">talks</span><span class="tag">presentations</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://m.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLkyaYNWEKcOf_C_6W45abNvXMb40xUUqh" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2019</a></div><div class="resource-description">2019 Demuxed talks &amp; presentations</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">talks</span><span class="tag">presentations</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLkyaYNWEKcOfD1GYFxFbZXDP03XM-cZPg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2021</a></div><div class="resource-description">2021 Demuxed talks &amp; presentations</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">talks</span><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">presentations</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLkyaYNWEKcOf98lZxnCcL6y7ZIVU3oSYO" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2022</a></div><div class="resource-description">2022 Demuxed talks &amp; presentations</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">video</span><span class="tag">talks</span><span class="tag">technology</span><span class="tag">streaming</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://2024.demuxed.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2024</a></div><div class="resource-description">Demuxed is a conference for video engineers focusing on video technology, encompassing topics from encoding to delivery and playback. Originating from the SF Video Technology meetup, it aims to create a community for engineers building the technology powering video. The event features discussions on various aspects of video engineering and is organized by a community-led group with support from Mux.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video engineering</span><span class="tag">conference</span><span class="tag">encoding</span><span class="tag">delivery</span><span class="tag">playback</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://2025.demuxed.com/live" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2025 (London) — Schedule</a></div><div class="resource-description">Official site for the 11th Demuxed, the first held outside the US, with the full two-day video-engineering talk schedule.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6bgPl4DFzzg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2025 Lightning Talks</a></div><div class="resource-description">Demuxed 2025 lightning-talk block including Clément Cordier&#39;s Pikimov web video engineering talk.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://2025.demuxed.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed 2025 — program and talk archive</a></div><div class="resource-description">Demuxed 2025 conference site with the full talk lineup and abstracts, covering Chromium native HLS, BFI FFV1/Matroska archival workflows, CMSD-based failure detection, and media-first CDN caching.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.demuxed.com/about" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed Conference</a></div><div class="resource-description">Engineer-run video-tech conference feeding the video-dev Slack community and city meetups.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.demuxed.com/meetups" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed Meetups Directory</a></div><div class="resource-description">Live directory of independently-run video-tech meetups worldwide (SF Video Tech, Paris Video Tech, Stockholm, Portland, etc).</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.demuxed.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed Podcast</a></div><div class="resource-description">Podcast for video engineers run by Heavybit, 22+ episodes covering DASH, HLS, RTMP, hls.js, Shaka Player, and low-latency streaming with guests from Bitmovin, Vimeo, VideoLAN, and Livepeer.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://2017.demuxed.com/meetups/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Demuxed — Global video engineering meetups index</a></div><div class="resource-description">Index of video-engineering meetups worldwide affiliated with Demuxed, spanning SF, London, NYC and other cities.</div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.meetup.com/Denver-Digital-Video/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Denver Video Technology Meetup</a></div><div class="resource-description">The Denver Video Technology meetup is for individuals interested in the technology behind video and video publishing, focusing on software development. Topics include video streaming, transcoding, codecs, and open standards, emphasizing the software aspects of video technology.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">streaming</span><span class="tag">transcoding</span><span class="tag">codec</span><span class="tag">software development</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.digitalfaq.com/forum/video/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Video Forum – The Digital FAQ</a></div><div class="resource-description">The Digital Video Forum on The Digital FAQ website offers discussions on DVD and Blu-ray creation, video hardware repair, videography, and blank media. It includes sub-forums for project planning, workflows, capturing, editing, encoding, and authoring, providing a comprehensive resource for developers and professionals in video streaming and encoding.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">video streaming</span><span class="tag">video encoding</span><span class="tag">video hardware</span><span class="tag">developer forum</span><span class="tag">video technology</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.dvinfo.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Video Information Network (DVinfo.net)</a></div><div class="resource-description">DVinfo.net is a platform offering forums and resources focused on digital video technology, including discussions on video cameras, editing software, and production techniques. It&#39;s a valuable resource for developers seeking information on video streaming and encoding technologies.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">digital video</span><span class="tag">video technology</span><span class="tag">forum</span><span class="tag">resources</span><span class="tag">community</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.dpreview.com/forums/1045" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Video Talk Forum</a></div><div class="resource-description">Hosted by Digital Photography Review, this forum is dedicated to discussions on digital video capture and processing, encompassing topics from digital still cameras to camcorders. It&#39;s a valuable resource for sharing knowledge and troubleshooting video-related issues.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">digital video</span><span class="tag">video processing</span><span class="tag">camcorders</span><span class="tag">video capture</span><span class="tag">community forum</span></div></div><div class="resource">
            <div class="resource-title"><a href="https://www.dpreview.com/forums/1009" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Digital Video Talk Forum on DPReview</a></div><div class="resource-description">The Digital Video Talk Forum on DPReview is a community where videographers and video editors discuss topics related to videography, video editing, and equipment. It&#39;s a valuable platform for sharing knowledge and seeking advice on video production.</div><div class="tags"><span class="tag">videography</span><span class="tag">video editing</span><span class="tag">forum</span><span class="tag">video production</span><span class="tag">community</span></div></div><div class="resource">
